          {
            title: 'Satat',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Satat is a trick-taking card game that involves tricks, trump, following suit. The game originated in Mauritius (related to Indian Seven Hands); name from Hindi "saat hant" (seven hands). Objective: win at least seven of 13 tricks.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Mauritius\nTime Period: Traditional; information from Mauritian source (Satat.net).\nHistorical Development: Related to the Indian game Seven Hands (Rang/Court Piece); name from Hindi "saat hant" (seven hands). Most popular card game in Mauritius.\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game in Mauritius.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
